This is a more detailed version of my point with regard to "no
controls"; for any community to properly function consistently, there
needs to be at least a _token_ method to enforce that community's
standards.  USENET provides none, and this is why traffic is finally 
slowing to a crawl everywhere but the binaries groups.

"Ignore the troll" has been tried and found wanting as well; in any
community sufficiently large, some well-meaning soul will always respond
to the troll.  Some deluded souls will also throw personal attacks out
against the troll; this just increases the noise without adding any
signal.  Again, with no method of enforcing that people both a) talk about
Nethack, and b) address the argument, not the arguer, the noise ratio
spirals rapidly beyond an acceptable level.

What many aren't really understanding here is the true scope of the
problem: that RGRN is not only no longer the center of the NH community 
and not the sole source for NH discussion -- it's the hardest one to get 
to now, and provides the least 'bang for the buck'.  It's not impossible 
to discuss things on USENET, just no longer worth the effort.

